### Page 1 of 22

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION APPROVING WATER AND SANITARY SEWER
SERVICES, BY OUTSIDE USER WATER AND SANITARY SEWER
SERVICES AGREEMENTS, FOR WYOMING KING GOLD MINING
COMPANY, INC., FOR ALL SECTION 36, T14N, R70W OF THE 6TH
P.M., LARAMIE COUNTY, WYOMING.”

WHEREAS, State of Wyoming is the owner of the property in Laramie County,
Wyoming, more specifically described as:

Section 36, Township 14 North, Range 70 West, of the 6th P.M., Laramie County,
Wyoming; and

WHEREAS, Wyoming King Gold Mining Company, Inc. (Gold King Corp) submitted
application to the Board of Public Utilities (“BOPU”) for water and sanitary sewer services
outside of the corporate limits of the City of Cheyenne for the above-referenced properties; and

WHEREAS, pursuant to Resolution No. 3577, BOPU was instructed to present to the
Governing Body for its review any application for the provision of water and/or sanitary sewer
services to any individual or entity outside the corporate limits of the City of Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS, BOPU has reviewed and approved the application submitted by Gold King
Corp, and BOPU and Gold King Corp will execute Outside User Water and Sanitary Sewer
Services Agreements upon approval by the Governing Body pursuant to Resolution No. 3577;
and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body has reviewed the applications for water and sanitary
sewer services submitted by Gold King Corp and has determined that approval is in the best
interest of the City of Cheyenne.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the application submitted by Gold King Corp to
BOPU for water and sanitary sewer services outside of the corporate limits of the City of
Cheyenne for the property described as Section 36, Township 14 North, Range 70 West, of the
6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming, is hereby approved.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that BOPU and Gold King Corp are authorized to
execute Outside User Water and Sanitary Sewer Services Agreements.

By Stefanie Boster at 10:16 am, Oct 05, 2022
```

