9.
System Development Fee: The Parties agree that GKshall pay a System Development Fee
prior to any connection to the South Crow Pipeline,36 Inch Pipeline, and water purchases from
the BOPU System begins.The System Development Fee will be calculated by using the“Large
Commercial/Industrial User" Base Demand rate of 600 gallons per minute times 37.8%.No 1.5
multiplier shallbe applied to this calculation based on the temporary usage being supplied to GK
and that GK water tap into theBOPU system and the pump station willbe abandoned and removed
upon completion of mining activities and reclamation, no later than January 1, 2037.The System
Development fee is being reduced to 37.8% because GK is purchasing raw water and not treated
water.
